<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Vikrant Goes to War, 1971</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;India vs. Pakistan in the Bay of Bengal, December 1971 - Final Scenario Version&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You are Commander, Eastern Fleet of the Republic of India's navy&amp;nbsp;with war against Pakistan coinsidered imminent. After&amp;nbsp;deliberate&amp;nbsp;preparations,&amp;nbsp;the Fleet&amp;nbsp;has sortied with your flagship &lt;EM&gt;INS Vikrant&lt;/EM&gt;&amp;nbsp;and you&amp;nbsp;have been briefed by the Chief of the Naval Staff on the&amp;nbsp;Chief of Naval Operations&amp;nbsp;intentions for your force. The text of this document will be found in the Scenario&amp;nbsp;Briefing. You will receive&amp;nbsp;the latest&amp;nbsp;intelligence summery sometime this morning.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Scenario Notes&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This scenario uses Submarine Communications, Aircraft Damage and has a script which determines daily aircraft serviceability. For the latter, every night at midnight local time (Zulu +6-hours), aircraft availability for the day&amp;nbsp;is determined. Availability for your air assets are ~70%, but as each aircraft is checked independently, overall availability may&amp;nbsp;appear greater or less. Unservicable aircraft are given a reserve loadout with a random time to ready between ten-hours and 23-hours 59-minutes so&amp;nbsp;some aircraft may become&amp;nbsp;usable throughout the day.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Vikrant&lt;/EM&gt; Goes to War&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&amp;nbsp;also models high-seas&amp;nbsp;visit, boarding, search and siezure (VBSS) operations as part of the Indian naval blockade of East Pakistan. If an Indian surface ship closes within ~200 metres of a merchant ship a script will be generated advising the Player of the nationality and cargo. Neutral shipping must not be interfered with but there are some ships of Pakistan registry, charters or naval auxiliaries that&amp;nbsp;may be siezed&amp;nbsp;if the Player's ship remains in very close proximity to the Pakistani ship until the siezure message fires and the ship changes sides. To receive Victory Points for siezed shipping they must be sent to the naval port of Visakhapatnam.&amp;nbsp;VBSS operations do not apply to fishing vessels, ferries, coastal or harbour craft whether of Pakistani registry or not.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Player has two Soviet-built &lt;EM&gt;Petya&lt;/EM&gt; small antisubmarine ships, which are currently tasked with blockade enforcement. They are performing duties that they were not really designed for and have a limited endurance&amp;nbsp;so may run into fuel shortages as the scenario proceeds. Although they are not fitted for RAS, the tanker &lt;EM&gt;INS Deepak A50&lt;/EM&gt; is in port at Visakhapatnam and has been "fitted" for gas-fuel replenishment. Move &lt;EM&gt;Deepak&lt;/EM&gt; within ~200 metres of&amp;nbsp;a &lt;EM&gt;Petya&lt;/EM&gt; and an event will fire to refuel their bunkers. When the evolution is complete, you will receive a message to that effect. Each ship may only RAS once.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The AA destroyers &lt;EM&gt;INS Beas&lt;/EM&gt; and &lt;EM&gt;INS Brahmaputra&lt;/EM&gt; also have very&amp;nbsp;poor endurance relative to the scenario length and there is a repeatable special action that will refuel them as necessary without any RAS stuff.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;A huge dept of thanks goes out to Forum Members "Stilesw" and "Whicker" for giving essential Lua scripting help to this funtional Lua illiterate during the scenario creation process. But all errors are mine.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Christopher Comars aka Randomizer&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;P.S. I do not know the creator(s) of the random aircraft maintenance Lua script but need to acknowledge them and their script with gratitude.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
